  not a config change.

  Concretely, [38;5;153mapp.js:5[39m already does [38;5;153mconsole.log("Logging in:", username)[39m. Most SaaS SDKs mirror [38;5;153mconsole.*[39m into
  breadcrumbs by default, so that line becomes a username in vendor storage the moment we install one. Whatever we pick,
  that line changes.

  - [1mErrors + explicit events, strict allowlist.[0m We call the logger deliberately; nothing is auto-captured. Buys
    certainty that no form value escapes; costs debugging power — you only see what someone predicted to log.
  - [1mErrors + masked breadcrumbs (recommended).[0m Auto-capture clicks, navigation, and network calls with all input values
    masked and [38;5;153mconsole[39m mirroring off, plus explicit domain events at the interesting points. Buys the
    reconstruct-the-session power that justifies the vendor; costs a config surface you have to get right and re-verify
    on SDK upgrades.
  - [1mFull session replay.[0m Buys the most diagnostic power; costs the largest privacy surface and a real consent/compliance
    conversation.
  - [1mUncaught errors only.[0m Buys near-zero risk and near-zero effort; costs everything about the flow — validation
    failures and failed logins produce no telemetry at all, and those are exactly the "production issues" that prompt
    this request.

  I recommend [1merrors + masked breadcrumbs[0m: it's the level where the vendor pays for itself, and the masking is a known,
  testable configuration rather than a judgment call at every call site.
